     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi all,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I’m very sorry for this basic question but I need some help\r\ninterpreting the output of the occuMulti function. I am trying to model the\r\noccupancy of two species (puma and collared peccary) in the presence of some\r\ndetection variables and occupancy variables. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I built the frame like this:<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">puma_peccary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">unmarkedFrameOccuMulti</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pumaoccupancy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> peccaryoccupancy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> siteCovs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">site</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> obsCovs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><u></u><u></u><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">So far so good. I made a “null” model assuming constant\r\ndetection and constant occupancy for both species like this:<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">m0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">occuMulti</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;~1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;~1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;~1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;~1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;~1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> puma_peccary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><u></u><u></u><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The output of this model looks like this:<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Occupancy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br><br>                      </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Estimate</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    SE      z P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&gt;|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">|)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sp1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Intercept</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0794</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.595</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.133</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.894</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sp2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Intercept</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2794</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.661</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.423</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.672</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sp1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sp2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Intercept</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.1282</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.866</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.303</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.193</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br> <br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Detection</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>                  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Estimate</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    SE     z  P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&gt;|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">|)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sp1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Intercept</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.842</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.160</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.26</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.41e-07</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sp2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Intercept</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.169</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.193</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6.07</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.32e-09</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br> <br><br> <br><br>AIC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">599.9831</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\"><br></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">From this output, I’m guessing sp1 is puma and sp2 is\r\ncollared peccary. Is it correct to conclude from this output that there is a\r\npositive correlation between the occupancy of puma and peccary (estimate\r\n1.1282). I understand this relation is not significant, I’m just trying to\r\nunderstand what the output tells me. <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am working on a set of candidate models that are designed\r\nto test the effects of certain detection variables and certain occupancy\r\nvariables, but if it’s possible I would like to add presence/absence of a\r\ncertain species to these terms as well. For example: does presence of puma have\r\nan influence on peccary detection? Is there any way I can include this?<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks for the help!<u></u><u></u></p></div>"
